From: Khem Raj <khem.raj@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 01:58:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] systemd: Fix narrowing conversion of msg_iovlen on musl

glibc declares struct msghdr::msg_iovlen as size_t, but musl declares
it as int. Initializing it directly from the size_t iovLen counter
therefore triggers a -Wc++11-narrowing error with clang on musl.
iovLen is bounded by the fixed-size 14-element iovec array, so an
explicit cast to int is safe and does not truncate any real value.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Khem Raj <khem.raj@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
--- a/src/common-lib/systemd.cpp
+++ b/src/common-lib/systemd.cpp
@@ -329,7 +329,7 @@
         .msg_name    = (struct ::sockaddr *) &sa,
         .msg_namelen = (socklen_t) (offsetof(struct sockaddr_un, sun_path) + ::strlen(sa.sun_path)),
         .msg_iov     = iov.data(),
-        .msg_iovlen  = iovLen,
+        .msg_iovlen  = static_cast<int>(iovLen),
         .msg_control = nullptr,
         .msg_controllen = 0,
         .msg_flags   = 0,
